L000215	Away from the set of $\ell=m$ modes, below we are interested also in the behavior of the system in the nonlinear regime, when keeping $m$ fixed, but considering modes with $\ell\geq m$. In Fig.~\ref{fig:indexspace}, we show the non-vanishing couplings between the lowest $\ell$-modes at fixed azimuthal index $m=1$. In this case, the non-vanishing coefficients no longer form a simple plane in index space, but rather a band with width $>1$. The coefficients $D^{mmmm}_{\bar{\ell}\ell\ell'\ell''}$ share these features for other fixed azimuthal indices $m\neq 1$ as well. In the eikonal limit $E^{1111}_{\bar{\ell}\ell\ell\ell}\sim \ell^{1/2}$ for fixed $\bar{\ell}$, while $D^{1111}_{\bar{\ell}\ell\ell\ell}\sim \ell^{-3/2}$. This is a signature of the scale-dependence of the derivative self-interactions compared with their potential-type counterparts.
